{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Jacob was left alone.</b> He had forgotten small jars and went back for them (Chullin 91)." "<b>And a man wrestled.</b> Menachem explains it as ״וַיִּתְעַפֵּר אִישׁ״ — a term of dust, for they would raise dust with their feet through their struggling. And it appears to me that it is a term of ״וַיִּתְקַשֵּׁר״, and it is an Aramaic expression: בָּתַר דַּאֲבִיקוּ בֵיהּ, וַאֲבֵיק לֵיהּ מֵיבַק — a term of binding, for so is the way of two who grapple to throw one another, that one embraces and wrestles him with his arms. And the Sages, of blessed memory, explained that he was the guardian angel of Esav (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:49.943083865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}